      "side": 1,
      "message": "`extra_cfg-\u003ematrix_coefficients`, `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_x`, and `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_y` are set by their own codec controls. Depending on the default values of these three `extra_cfg` options, it may take multiple `aom_codec_control()` calls to set `extra_cfg-\u003ematrix_coefficients` to `AOM_CICP_MC_IDENTITY` and both `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_x` and `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_y` to 0. So this check in `validate_config()` could be overly strict because the transient states before the final ``aom_codec_control()` call would be considered invalid.\n\nFortunately the default values of `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_x` and `extra_cfg-\u003echroma_subsampling_y` are both 0. So right now only an `aom_codec_control` call to set `extra_cfg-\u003ematrix_coefficients` to `AOM_CICP_MC_IDENTITY` is needed and we don\u0027t need to go through invalid transient states.",
